      {
        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 5,
        "titulo": "Gender from the ending",
        "explicacao": "Every Russian noun has a grammatical gender, and you can usually read it from the last letter. Masculine: a consonant (друг, стол). Feminine: -а / -я (подруга, машина). Neuter: -о / -е (окно, море). English has «he», «she» and «it» only for people and animals; in Russian even a table or a window has a gender. The possessive (my, your…) must match the gender of the noun that follows it.",
        "exemplos": [
          {
            "ru": "мой друг",
            "pt": "my friend (male)"
          },
          {
            "ru": "моя подруга",
            "pt": "my friend (female)"
          },
          {
            "ru": "моё окно",
            "pt": "my window"
          },
          {
            "ru": "мои друзья",
            "pt": "my friends"
          }
        ]
